// The typed IR (`ctxc ir`) of `e ifoverflow x`: an `ovf` whose flag, a local, is the one each
// arithmetic operation of e sets; and ctxc's reader and printer give the same text back.
//# build text: {home}/tests/helpers/text.ctx

//# $ {text} to p.ir {ctxc} ir {std} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0

// The flag's number, `{a}`, is the same in the three places.
//# $ {text} count p.ir "(ovf {n} {a} (arith {n} add (arith {n} mul {any} {a}) {any} {a}) "
//# stdout:
//| 1

//# $ {text} to q.ir {ctxc} roundtrip p.ir
//# exit: 0
//# $ {text} same p.ir q.ir
//# stdout:
//| same
